* twig wood density (TWD)
* g/cm^3
* individual
* mean
* 1
* Branch segments (1.5–4 cm diameter, 10 cm long) were collected from the outer canopy of each sampled individual. We removed bark and fresh volume was determined using the water displacement method. Each twig sample was then split into half and the heartwood of the samples was removed. Samples were oven-dried at 70°C for at least 72 hours until reaching constant mass, and dry mass was recorded to the nearest 0.001 g. Wood density was calculated as oven-dried mass divided by fresh volume. 

